<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Heavenfield</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">634</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Heavenfield was fought in 634 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hexham">Hexham</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northumberland">Northumberland</a>, where Oswald of Bernicia defeated and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cadwallon-ap-cadfan">Cadwallon ap Cadfan</a> of Gwynedd, who had ravaged Northumbria after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hatfield-chase">Battle of Hatfield Chase</a>. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bede">Bede</a>, Oswald raised a wooden cross before the battle. The victory reunited Northumbria under Oswald, who brought Irish missionaries from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iona">Iona</a> to convert his kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-heavenfield.jpg" alt="Battle of Heavenfield" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Dixon · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cross_at_Heavenfield_(geograph_3191606).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
